repository-code: 'https://github.com/hawkij/ZERCalc'
abstract: >-
  ZER-Calc is a Python-based model to aggregate energy
  resource demands of net-zero emissions plans across
  sectors and industries. All energy demands depend on three
  Zero Emissions Resources (ZERs): emissions-free
  electricity, carbon storage and biomass. These aggregated
  demands for ZERs are calculated by ZER-Calc so they can be
  compared against estimates of 2050 probable ZER supply. 
keywords:
